{#- Routing pointer for code-absent project facts (SPEC-mission-context-loop AC-005, ADR-002).

    ONE source for the four claude-md variants, AGENTS.md and the Cursor rule. Claude Code's
    documented default sends "remember X" to machine-local auto-memory; this line is what
    routes a shared project fact to the git-shared wiki instead, even when the skill does not
    trigger. SPEC-maker-front-door-improvements AC-004 / ADR-006: the skill is typed-only now
    (not model-invocable), so every arm names the world-model invocation and the procedure FILE
    instead of "follow the skill". AC-005 caps the rendered section at 300 characters per variant
    (at HANDLE_MAX) and requires `project-knowledge` and `auto-memory`: every always-loaded
    byte is carried every turn. The heading stays English in both locales so the section is
    locatable, as `context_discipline.md.j2` does. `is_codex` is guarded because some callers
    render AGENTS.md.j2 directly without it (it is path-derived only inside `synthesize`). -#}
{%- set wm = config.world_model if (config is defined and config.world_model is defined and config.world_model) else {"name": "Maker", "handle": "maker"} -%}
{%- set codex = is_codex is defined and is_codex -%}
{%- set inv = ("$" if codex else "/") ~ wm.handle -%}
{%- set proc = (".agents" if codex else ".claude") ~ "/skills/project-knowledge/SKILL.md" -%}
## Project knowledge

{% if not codex and (config.locale | default('en')) == 'ko' -%}
코드에 없는 프로젝트 사실의 기록·정정은 `{{ inv }}` 로 — `{{ proc }}` 를 읽고 따른다. 사실은 auto-memory 가 아니라 `.claude/memory/wiki.md` 에 (auto-memory 는 개인 선호만).
{%- else -%}
To remember or fix a project fact the code does not show, use `{{ inv }}`, which reads `{{ proc }}`: facts go to `.claude/memory/wiki.md`, not host auto-memory (personal preferences only).
{%- endif %}
